# Ìdíléwa — workspace rules

## Rule 0 — verify the stack before applying a brief

This repository is a **static HTML/CSS/JS site** bundled by Vite:

- `index.html` + ~31 sibling `.html` pages (in-page sections switched by the
  global `go(id)` helper, standalone pages linked as `/login`, `/pricing`, …).
- `app.js` — vanilla router/renderers for the Vue-less shell pages.
- `styles.css` — legacy shared styles. `design-system.css` — the current layer.
- `src/server/*` + `api/*` — serverless AI endpoints (Node, ESM).
- Dependencies: `@supabase/supabase-js`, `canvas-confetti`, `convex`, `three`,
  `vite`. **No React, no JSX, no Tailwind, no Framer Motion, no lucide-react.**

If an instruction assumes React/Tailwind, translate it into the vanilla
equivalent and say so in the response. Never install a package that no bundle
imports.

## Design work

`AWESOME_DESIGN.md` is the source of truth. Read it before touching UI.

- **UI/UX Pro Max** → hierarchy, spacing rhythm, contrast, responsive states.
  Apply via the tokens in `design-system.css` (`--id-*`). No new raw hex values
  in component rules.
- **Impeccable** → motion discipline. CSS transitions only, `--id-ease` /
  `--id-ease-spring`, animate `opacity`/`transform`, always ship a
  `prefers-reduced-motion` fallback.
- **Taste Skill** → anti-slop. No neon, no emoji in buttons or nav, no raw
  Unicode arrows, no filler marketing verbs, no decorative "developer notes" in
  body copy.
- **Framer Motion is not available.** Use CSS transitions + `IntersectionObserver`
  (see `setupReveal` in `src/siteNav.js`) for stagger/entrance.
- **lucide-react is not available.** Use inline `<svg>` (24×24, stroke 2, round
  caps) or a `mask-image` data-URI, as in the `.featureTile` icon chips.
- Exactly three button tiers: `.id-btn--primary`, `.id-btn--outline`,
  `.id-btn--ghost`, plus `.id-icon-btn` for icon-only controls. One primary
  button per view.
- Interactive behaviour for the header/drawer/reveals belongs in
  `src/siteNav.js`; markup hooks are `data-id-*`, `data-open`, `data-state`.
  Keep every hook guarded — the script runs on pages without a header.

## Editing conventions

- `index.html` and `app.js` contain very long single-line blocks with inline
  base64 images. Prefer exact-string PowerShell `.Replace()` (with a match
  count check) or `IndexOf`/`Substring` edits over line-based rewrites.
- Preserve Yorùbá diacritics exactly in user-facing strings.
- `go(id)` only accepts ids of `main > section` elements that exist in the page
  (`home`, `academy`, `studio`, `tutors`, `codeLab`, `aiChat`, `progress`,
  `heritageLab`, `discoveryGames`, …). Added `voices` routes exist only in
  `app.js`-driven shells — do not call `go('voices')` from `index.html`.
- No secrets in client code. AI keys stay server-side in `api/*` + `src/server/*`
  and are read from `process.env` inside the handler.

## AI providers

- `src/server/aiConversation.js` dispatches by `AI_PROVIDER` (`gemini` |
  `ollama`, default `ollama`). Gemini transport lives in
  `src/server/geminiProvider.js` (REST, `x-goog-api-key`, no SDK).
- Env: `AI_PROVIDER`, `GEMINI_API_KEY` (or `GOOGLE_AI_API_KEY`), `GEMINI_MODEL`,
  optional `GEMINI_BASE_URL`, `GEMINI_EMBEDDING_MODEL`. Never log the key.
- Failures must surface as explicit non-success responses (429 rate limit, 400
  rejected credentials, 404 retired/unavailable model, 5xx upstream). Never
  fabricate a reply.
- `.env` is local-only and git-ignored. Production values live in Vercel.

## Verification before finishing

```powershell
npm test        # must stay green (the full node --test suite)
npm run build   # Vite must exit 0
```

Add tests for new behaviour (`node --test`, `node:assert/strict`, `fetchImpl`
injection for network calls). Then check `git status` for stray temp files
(`_*.ps1`, `_*.mjs`, `_*.txt`) and delete them before committing.
